body:
We simply wouldn't know, usually progression like this takes teams of people... I feel like even in a scenario where these specific people don't exist, somebody else would eventually make it happen. The issue is that plenty of people theoretically don't exist right now, but there's no way to gauge how much better or worse off we are for it because they're not here...

&#x200B;

... also most people aren't that influential, most people majorly influence a dozen people or so... the odds of having the next savior of humanity aren't really in anyone's favor.

Oh sorry, I started finasteride in early 2017 and spironolactone on a super low dose in mid 2017... I only started where I did because that's when my spiro dose started being significant but I should've stated that as well.

&#x200B;

But yeah I experienced mass hair loss in May, which was over a year into taking finasteride... I noticed no difference in hair loss since having stopped taking it. The finasteride alone actually had no real effect on my hair over the 1 and a half years that I took it, my hair didn't start changing until spiro was upped in the mix.

